{"availability":"available","full":"Wgmlgz/zhaba-script","name":"zhaba-script","description":"Zhaba script - is a multi-paradigm, high-level, statically typed, interpreted or source to source compiled language, which focuses at minimizing programs size and maximizing development speed and comfort..","category":"Developer tools","language":"C++","stars":13,"forks":1,"created":"2021-06-18T01:01:15Z","updated":"2022-07-11T09:25:07Z","license":"GPL-3.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://wgmlgz.github.io/zhaba/","topics":["c","compiler","cpp","cpp20","frog","language","programming-language"],"demo":"https://wgmlgz.github.io/zhaba/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T21:05:34.085Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T21:05:34.085Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T21:05:34.085Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T21:05:34.085Z","stars":13,"forks":1}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Zhaba-script (Russian: ˈʐabə, жаба(toad)) - is a multi-paradigm, high-level, statically typed, interpreted or source to source compiled language, designed to be as performant as C, but as beautiful as Python.","The syntax of zhaba-script is the most interesting and different feature from other programming languages. It basically resembles python, which uses indents instead of curly brackets to declare code blocks. But zhaba-script takes a step forward by making many syntactic elements, such as commas, optional. For example, in the expression: print(1, 2, 4) it is obvious where the commas should be, and zhaba-script makes them optional in some places. Other syntactic elements, such as colons or semicolons, are also optional. In addition, the most common keywords in other languages, such as if or…","Semantically, the language is similar to such system languages as C, C++ or Rust. Like C, zhaba-script provides low-level memory control and combines it with so-called zero-cost abstractions. For example, among them are references, function overloading, template types, constructors and destructors."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Wgmlgz/zhaba-script/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"de07deaa6628471b9b49b16e078d4af28d8bcd9e470270799debaabbecfa1c02","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T21:05:34.242Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T21:05:34.242Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Zhaba-script (Russian: ˈʐabə, жаба(toad)) - is a multi-paradigm, high-level, statically typed, interpreted or source to source compiled language, designed to be as performant as C, but as beautiful as Python.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Wgmlgz/zhaba-script/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"de07deaa6628471b9b49b16e078d4af28d8bcd9e470270799debaabbecfa1c02","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Wgmlgz/zhaba-script/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T21:05:34.244Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2022-07-11T09:25:07Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Wgmlgz/zhaba-script/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T21:05:34.248Z","hash":"de07deaa6628471b9b49b16e078d4af28d8bcd9e470270799debaabbecfa1c02","originalBytes":77554,"storedBytes":77554,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["out","zhaba-script","type","vec","int","std","functions","file","end","str","function","vector","example","lop","range","name","string","types","slf","begin","like","content","standard","using","constructor","library","other","variable","when","which","map","some","syntax","ctor","element","outputs","block","compiler","description","exit","exp","here","iterator","iterators","used","examples","get","them","val","veciter","operator","panic","avliter","code","create","main","member","need","result","want","access","generic","line","most","only","returns","any","err","import","json","put","such","test","c++","cur","doesn","errors","language","return","run","size","strr","sub","value","write","allows","avltree","bool","bytecode","char","data","definition","different",